  Each translated URL is annotated with the whole language cluster it belongs
  to, itself included. Google requires every URL in a set to list every alternate - a
  one-way annotation is ignored outright - and the same reciprocity is repeated
  in the <link rel="alternate"> tags in each page's <head>. x-default points at
  the English URL, which is where a visitor with no matching language
  preference should land.

  <lastmod> is the only optional field kept. Google reads it, but only from
  sitemaps whose dates it has learned to trust, so it must reflect a real change
  to that page - bumping all eight on every deploy is what makes it ignored.
  <changefreq> and <priority> are omitted: Google states it ignores both.

  URLs match the canonical tag on each page exactly: clean /privacy without the
  .html, and a trailing slash on the project directories.
-->
